    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="1016" n="1004" xml:id="pg1004"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/5–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-18T09:00:00+03:00">May 18, 1945—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1639. Today’s papers published brief item quoting Secretary’s statement<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d755-f1"/> that Lend-Lease deliveries will be continued in
                    amounts necessary for achieving quick and final victory with minimum losses and
                    that no other consideration than changing military situation will dictate
                    changes in Lend-Lease program after defeat of Germany.</p>
                <p>Nothing has appeared in Under Secretary’s statement<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d755-f2"/> regarding reduction in Lend-Lease program for Soviet
                    Union.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d755-f1" n="55" xml:id="d755-f1-content">
                <p>Made at San Francisco, May 15, 1945, Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, May 20, 1945, p. 940.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d755-f2" n="56" xml:id="d755-f2-content">
                <p>Released May 14, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
